R3 CONFIRMATION PATCHES
These clauses are additive and controlling over R2 where applicable.

R3-C1 — EMERGENCY / CONSTITUTIONAL BLOCKING PRECEDENCE
When an emergency trigger is UNKNOWN, INCOMPLETE, or non-admitted because its applicable qualified evidence profile is absent or unresolved, that emergency condition cannot override, bypass, or locally downgrade any current VETO, VIOLATION, or other blocking ConstitutionalEvent / Constitution / Policy / AAP consequence. The blocking consequence retains precedence and the emergency path remains non-admitted until its required evidence/profile conditions are satisfied under existing authority and safety rules.

R3-C2 — CONSENT VALIDITY IS NECESSARY, NEVER SUFFICIENT
ConsentValidityDisposition=VALID_FOR_SCOPE is necessary where consent is required, but never sufficient for action admission. If any separately applicable rights, law, safety, policy, authority, capability, privacy, or evidence gate is UNKNOWN, INCONCLUSIVE, STALE, INVALID, or BLOCKED, the composed action disposition remains non-admitted regardless of consent validity. Consent cannot promote another unresolved hard gate to PASS.

R3-C3 — ACTIVEDEFINITIONINDEX RELEASE-MANIFEST BINDING
The ActiveDefinitionIndex / EffectiveSemanticSnapshot is a hash-bound first-class release-interpretation artifact under ZR-006. Its own artifact hash SHALL be recorded in ReleaseManifest, and its entries SHALL bind exact normative source ranges/hashes. Mutation of a bound normative source range without index regeneration makes the index STALE/INVALID. The index remains derived metadata and cannot override normative source.

