ZR-005 — DERIVED ACTIVE-DEFINITION / EFFECTIVE-SEMANTIC INDEX

Problem:
Append-only lineage leaves obsolete review/status prose early in the final files, making current state difficult for a new reader/parser to resolve.

R2 repair:
Add a hash-bound ActiveDefinitionIndex / EffectiveSemanticSnapshot as a DERIVED RELEASE INDEX, not a normative semantic owner.

For each active anchor/package it records:
- anchor/package ID
- owning layer/owner
- effective semantic version/status
- active source range/hash
- parent/child or alias/group relation
- superseded/inactive lineage refs
- active unresolved/deferred obligations
- release assurance dimensions

Rules:
- existing normative source + current-reading/precedence rules remain authoritative;
- if snapshot conflicts with normative source, the snapshot is defective and cannot override it;
- retained staged/candidate/review prose is explicitly HISTORICAL_INACTIVE / TRACEABILITY_ONLY as applicable;
- lineage is not deleted.

