ZR-006 — NORMATIVE SEMANTICS VS REVIEW EVIDENCE

R2 repair:
1. Review packets, reviewer/model outputs, review IDs, hashes and synthesis artifacts are TRACEABILITY_EVIDENCE_ONLY.
2. They are not normative semantic sources and cannot supply authority.
3. Every admitted semantic delta must be materialized in final normative source under an active owner/anchor.
4. CurrentReadingMap, UpgradeTraceabilityTable, ReleaseManifest and equivalent artifacts required to interpret/validate a release must be embedded or bundled as hash-bound first-class release artifacts.
5. Loss/unavailability of review evidence may degrade assurance/auditability, but it cannot cause normative meaning to migrate into an external packet.

This supersedes any wording that a reviewer packet is itself "part of the semantic reading"; the packet may be part of the EVIDENCE READING only.

