ZR-010 — THEORYARTIFACT METADATA + DERIVED THEORY RELEASE INDEX

Do not create a new theory Engine or independent second theory registry.

Extend the existing owner-qualified TheoryArtifact/current theory registry metadata with:
- semantic_role / artifact_kind
- current_effective_semantic_version
- release_effective_status
- validation_mode / evidence class
- owner/source anchor
- supersedes/refines lineage
- applicability conditions/falsifiers

Use a small closed registry enum with OTHER fallback rather than uncontrolled labels.
Initial semantic-role families MAY include:
MODELING_FRAMEWORK_OR_ONTOLOGY
STATE_THEORY
CONTROL_OR_REGULATION_THEORY
EFFECTIVE_DOMAIN_THEORY
SAFETY_CONTROL_ARCHITECTURE
EPISTEMIC_GOVERNANCE_ARCHITECTURE
REFERENCE_ARCHITECTURE
RESEARCH_FRAMEWORK
OTHER

A TheoryReleaseIndex near the top of the Theories layer is a DERIVED VIEW of the existing registry, not a second owner.
It must make the effective version/status of SRT, VSM, RPM, PPM, TFT, FET, SCT and reference/research profiles directly visible.
A theory/ref-architecture version is bumped only when its owned semantics change; release-level refinements that do not change the owned theory body are recorded as REFINE_BINDING/REFINE_COMPOSITION rather than fake semantic-version increments.

