ZR-011 — PROFILE-BIND REFERENCE-ARCHITECTURE OPERATIONAL CONSTANTS

For every active reference-architecture operational numeric constant:
A) bind it to a versioned qualified parameter/profile with scope/evidence, OR
B) mark it ILLUSTRATIVE_REFERENCE_DEFAULT / NON_NORMATIVE.

This includes, where not otherwise safety-case bound:
coverage alerts, cold-start coverage, availability/error/latency incident thresholds, degrade/recover windows, retry counts, reference consensus cardinalities and similar operational defaults.

Rules:
- Domain/safety constants already bound to an admitted safety case/profile remain enforceable within that scope.
- Reference defaults never silently become universal Garden invariants.
- Release validation flags unclassified operational constants.

===============================================================================
ZR-012 — EXTEND SEMANTICANCHOR METADATA; NO NEW DEFINITIONRECORD ONTOLOGY

Use the existing SemanticAnchor/declaration system.

Requirements:
- every ACTIVE definition has exactly one resolvable owner declaration;
- contentless/group anchors are explicitly ALIAS_OF or GROUP_REF;
- backlinks are typed references and never competing definitions;
- active source range/hash and status are machine-resolvable through the release index;
- large units MAY receive additive child-unit IDs/ranges when an objective decomposition rule is met; child indexing must not alter semantics;
- existing adjacency-resolved anchors are migrated by explicit alias/group declaration, not reinterpreted.

No new foundational DefinitionRecord object is required unless later implementation proves the existing anchor registry cannot carry these fields.

